WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.002
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.302 --> 00:00:08.584
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.884 --> 00:00:13.974
Unit twelve: When I Was Little. In this unit, you will talk about things you used to do.

4
00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:15.706
Little.

5
00:00:16.406 --> 00:00:18.254
Little means small or young.

6
00:00:18.554 --> 00:00:21.030
When I was little, I was afraid of the dark.

7
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.709
Your turn. Say: Little.

8
00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:27.085
Little.

9
00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:29.050
Used to.

10
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.282
Used to means did something often in the past, but not now.

11
00:00:33.582 --> 00:00:34.977
I used to cry a lot.

12
00:00:35.677 --> 00:00:38.074
Your turn. Say: Used to.

13
00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:41.694
Used to.

14
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:43.580
Toy.

15
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.233
Toy means a thing children play with.

16
00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:48.312
My favourite toy was a bear.

17
00:00:49.012 --> 00:00:51.653
Your turn. Say: Toy.

18
00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.098
Toy.

19
00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:56.736
Baby.

20
00:00:57.436 --> 00:00:59.517
Baby means a very young child.

21
00:00:59.817 --> 00:01:01.805
This is a photo of me as a baby.

22
00:01:02.505 --> 00:01:04.855
Your turn. Say: Baby.

23
00:01:07.555 --> 00:01:08.220
Baby.

24
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:10.136
Remember.

25
00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:13.289
Remember means to keep something in your mind.

26
00:01:13.589 --> 00:01:15.495
I remember my first day at school.

27
00:01:16.195 --> 00:01:19.138
Your turn. Say: Remember.

28
00:01:21.838 --> 00:01:22.770
Remember.

29
00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:24.587
Photo.

30
00:01:25.287 --> 00:01:27.229
Photo means a picture made with a camera.

31
00:01:27.529 --> 00:01:29.470
Mum keeps all my baby photos.

32
00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.103
Your turn. Say: Photo.

33
00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:35.676
Photo.

34
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:37.499
Grow up.

35
00:01:38.199 --> 00:01:40.442
Grow up means to become older and bigger.

36
00:01:40.742 --> 00:01:42.776
I want to be a teacher when I grow up.

37
00:01:43.476 --> 00:01:45.838
Your turn. Say: Grow up.

38
00:01:48.538 --> 00:01:49.261
Grow up.

39
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.089
Change.

40
00:01:51.789 --> 00:01:53.533
Change means to become different.

41
00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:55.484
My life has changed a lot.

42
00:01:56.184 --> 00:01:58.778
Your turn. Say: Change.

43
00:02:01.478 --> 00:02:02.421
Change.

44
00:02:03.417 --> 00:02:05.416
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:05.716 --> 00:02:08.296
Sreypich, what did you use to do when you were little?

46
00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:11.467
I used to sleep with a toy bear.

47
00:02:12.783 --> 00:02:15.447
That's sweet! Did you use to cry a lot?

48
00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.099
Yes! My mum says I used to cry every night.

49
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:23.244
Do you remember your first school?

50
00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:27.469
A little. I remember my teacher's kind smile.

51
00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:31.932
Grammar focus: Used to plus verb.

52
00:02:32.232 --> 00:02:35.326
I used to have a toy bear. I used to cry a lot.

53
00:02:35.626 --> 00:02:39.622
'Used to' is for things that were true in the past but are not true now.

54
00:02:40.617 --> 00:02:43.455
Now read and listen. Looking at Old Photos.

55
00:02:43.755 --> 00:02:46.474
Last night, my mother showed me my baby photos.

56
00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:50.352
When I was little, I used to sleep with a toy bear.

57
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.509
I used to be afraid of dogs, but now I love them.

58
00:02:55.817 --> 00:02:58.281
I remember playing in the rain with my brother.

59
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:02.338
I have grown up a lot, and many things have changed!

60
00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.198
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:06.498 --> 00:03:08.056
I blank to have long hair.

62
00:03:08.356 --> 00:03:11.464
A, used. B, use. C, using.

63
00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.939
The answer is A: used.

64
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.450
A very young child is a blank.

65
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:24.101
A, baby. B, toy. C, photo.

66
00:03:28.117 --> 00:03:30.325
The answer is A: baby.

67
00:03:31.817 --> 00:03:33.828
To become older and bigger is to blank.

68
00:03:34.128 --> 00:03:38.327
A, grow up. B, remember. C, change.

69
00:03:42.317 --> 00:03:44.038
The answer is A: grow up.

70
00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:48.992
Now it's your turn to speak. What did you use to do when you were little?

71
00:03:54.292 --> 00:03:59.194
When I was little, I used to play with dolls, and I used to be afraid of the dark.

72
00:03:59.494 --> 00:04:01.261
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:06.214
Great work today! You learned eight new words and used to plus verb.

74
00:04:06.514 --> 00:04:10.676
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

75
00:04:10.976 --> 00:04:13.872
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:14.172 --> 00:04:16.906
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

